  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C) and position a rack in the middle.",
    "Rinse the mulukhiyah leaves and pat dry with a paper towel.",
    "Heat the olive oil in the clay tajine over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and sauté until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and cook for another minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the chicken breast and cook until browned on all sides, about 5-6 minutes.",
    "Pour in the milk, add the flour, cumin, salt, and black pepper. Stir to combine.",
    "Add the mulukhiyah leaves, cover the clay tajine with a lid, and transfer it to the preheated oven.",
    "Bake for 20-25 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and the mulukhiyah is tender.",
    "Sprinkle with parmesan cheese and serve hot."
